# results/ holds raw outputs. The run JSONs are committed: Appendix B of the
# paper names them row by row, and a provenance table pointing at files nobody
# can open is not provenance. 19 files, about 2 MB.
#
# The per-run directories are NOT committed, and most no longer exist on any
# machine. Appendix B names those rows rather than listing them as if they were
# available.
results/*
!results/*.md
!results/*.json
!results/summaries/

# The tidy table is the per-measurement record every chart and table is drawn
# from, so it is committed for the same reason the run JSONs are: a figure whose
# underlying rows nobody can open is not evidence.
!results/tidy/
!results/tidy/*.csv

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# bearing writes its own outcome ledger; it is a record, so it is kept

# The citation sweep's raw cache is 8.9 MB of Semantic Scholar's records, not
# ours, and one command rebuilds it. The screened result beside it is small and
# is the thing the thread cites, so that one is committed.
results/R-004-rome-citers.json
